    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.files\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nWhen I open a .tsx file  with the mini.files plugin having the preview window option enabled and open the file, I notice that there is missing syntax highlighting and the comment plugin behaves differently than configured. However, when I disable the preview option, the file opens normally, and the syntax highlighting + commenting works as expected.\r\n\r\nNot sure if this is actually a mini.files issue or a treesitter plugin issue, but its behavior is unexpected for me considering it behaves as I expect it to with the preview option disabled.\r\n\r\nI also don't encounter this issue when using telescope (find files) or oil.nvim which also have preview features.\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\nNVIM v0.9.1\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n\r\n1. Open React + Typescript project with neovim. `nvim -nu minimal.lua .` \r\n2. (mini.files opens) Navigate to a `.tsx` component within a `src/` directory. This should cause a preview window to pop up, showing the hovered file.\r\n3. Open the file with by pressing the `l` key\r\n4. Observe missing/different highlighting than when the preview option is disabled.\r\n\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n\r\n<summary>minimal.lua</summary>\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal lazypath = vim.fn.stdpath(\"data\") .. \"/lazy/lazy.nvim\"\r\nif not vim.loop.fs_stat(lazypath) then\r\n    vim.fn.system({\r\n\t\"git\",\r\n\t\"clone\",\r\n\t\"--filter=blob:none\",\r\n\t\"https://github.com/folke/lazy.nvim.git\",\r\n\t\"--branch=stable\", -- latest stable release\r\n\tlazypath,\r\n    })\r\nend\r\nvim.opt.rtp:prepend(lazypath)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nrequire('lazy').setup({\r\n\r\n\r\n    {\r\n\t'nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter',\r\n\r\n\tdependencies = {\r\n\t    'JoosepAlviste/nvim-ts-context-commentstring',\r\n\t},\r\n\r\n\topts = {\r\n\r\n\t    ensure_installed = { 'typescript', 'tsx', 'javascript', 'html', 'css' },\r\n\r\n\t        context_commentstring = {\r\n\t\t enable = true,\r\n\t\t enable_autocmd = false\r\n\t\t    },\r\n\t\thighlight = {\r\n\t\t    enable = true\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t    },\r\n\t    main = \"nvim-treesitter.configs\"\r\n\t},\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\t{\r\n\t    'echasnovski/mini.comment',\r\n\t    version = '*',\r\n\t    opts = {\r\n\t\toptions = {\r\n\t\t    -- use integration with nvim-ts-context-commentstring\r\n\t\t    custom_commentstring = function()\r\n\t\t\treturn require('ts_context_commentstring.internal').calculate_commentstring() or vim.bo.commentstring\r\n\t\t    end,\r\n\t\t},\r\n\t    }\r\n\r\n\t},\r\n\r\n\r\n\t{\r\n\t    'echasnovski/mini.files',\r\n\t    version = false,\r\n\r\n\t    opts = {\r\n\t\twindows = {\r\n\t\t    -- NOTE:\r\n\t\t    -- Syntax highlighting is different in .tsx files when file is opened via the plugin and the preview option is enabled.\r\n\t\t    -- Also the comments revert back to default comment behavior instead of using the treesitter context aware comments.\r\n\t\t    preview = true,\r\n\t\t    width_focus = 30,\r\n\t\t    width_preview = 30,\r\n\t\t},\r\n\t\toptions = {\r\n\t\t    use_as_default_explorer = true,\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t    },\r\n\r\n\t    lazy = false,\r\n\r\n\t    keys = {\r\n\t\t{\r\n\t\t    \"<Leader>e\",\r\n\t\t    function()\r\n\t\t\tprint(\"Minus command ran!\")\r\n\t\t\trequire('mini.files').open(vim.loop.cwd(), true)\r\n\t\t    end,\r\n\t\t    desc = \"Open mini.files at cwd\"\r\n\t\t},\r\n\t\t{\r\n\t\t    \"-\",\r\n\t\t    function()\r\n\t\t\trequire('mini.files').open(vim.api.nvim_buf_get_name(0), true)\r\n\t\t    end,\r\n\t\t    desc = \"Open mini.files at current buf dir.\"\r\n\t\t},\r\n\t    },\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\t},\r\n\r\n\r\n\t-- No issues, when opening a file after using the \"actions.preview\" action\r\n\r\n\r\n\t-- {\r\n\t    --   'stevearc/oil.nvim',\r\n\t    --   lazy = false,\r\n\t    --   keys = {\r\n\t\t-- \t  {\"-\", \"<CMD>Oil<CR>\", desc = \"Open parent directory\"},\r\n\t\t--   },\r\n\t\t--   opts = {},\r\n\t\t--   -- Optional dependencies\r\n\t\t--   dependencies = { \"nvim-tree/nvim-web-devicons\" },\r\n\t\t-- }\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\t    })\r\n\r\n```\r\n</details\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nI expect the behavior to be consistent with the behavior when the preview option is disabled. When the preview window is enabled, the syntax highlighting should work and be detected properly.\r\n\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nWhen the preview window is enabled, the syntax highlighting is missing for .tsx files. However, when the preview option is disabled, the syntax highlighting works as expected.\r\n\r\n",
