        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This should be now fixed on latest `main`.\r\n\r\nThe reason seemed to be that 'mini.files' was trying to highlight lines from that file (almost unrelated to the future buffer, by the way) using `vim.treesitter.start()` with \"language\" `typescriptreact` (which is what the correct `filetype` option) instead of `tsx` (which is the correct \"language\").\r\n\r\nWith this fix highlighting and commenting seem to be tree-sitter aware. Could you, please, test it on your side and tell if it also works for you? Thanks!",
            "created_at": "2023-09-07T12:28:48Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/469#issuecomment-1710064136",
